{"date": "2026-10-31", "word": "Flat", "summary": "A flat day (forecast flat). Thermals stayed flat all day. The upslope ran from about 08:15 to about 16:00. A low day for October: the base stayed down near 3,700 ft (normal 4,500\u20135,400 ft). The evening before, the page called it normal, about 4,100 ft, a miss. Midday the base averaged about 3,700 ft by the Kekoa camera, 400 ft lower than the evening's number; the morning update said about 3,800 ft, off by 100 ft. Most of the day the shear line was on Makawao Avenue near Makawao, running toward Kahului; furthest north about 09:06, north of Pukalani, reaching the coast near Haiku; furthest south about 08:28, crossing Kula Highway between the middle Lower Kula Road junction and Waiakoa. Data gaps: Nakula stopped at 14:15; the Mesonet could not be reached on 26 of 88 updates.", "therm": "<strong>Flat</strong> for the day, 10:00\u201314:00<div class=\"sub\">Kula Ag's measured air through the NAM sounding (thermal.py); forecast was Flat</div>", "base": "", "notes": ["Saturated, dew-fed morning: low cloud until about 08:15.", "Base held flat at about 3,400 ft from 13:45 for about 4 hours.", "Watched for: Base will lift (P3) from 07:29."], "chart": "<div class=\"watch\"><div class=\"kind\">What the day did</div><ul><li>Saturated, dew-fed morning: low cloud until about 08:15.</li><li>Base held flat at about 3,400 ft from 13:45 for about 4 hours.</li><li>Watched for: Base will lift (P3) from 07:29.</li></ul></div><div style=\"font-weight:600;font-size:.9rem;margin:10px 0 2px\">Cloudbase</div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap;font-size:.8rem;color:var(--muted,#6b6b66);margin:2px 0 4px\">\n<span><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:16px;border-top:2px dashed #8a5cd6;vertical-align:middle\"></span> Forecast (sounding)</span>\n<span><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:16px;height:2px;background:#2a78d6;vertical-align:middle\"></span> Derived (stations)</span><span><span style=\"display:inline-block;w